@@ -6,14 +6,14 @@ Binding behaviour lives in `.feature` specs and referenced `assets/**`. History
 
 ## Defect under sail
 
-The external browser acceptance suite (real browser, Cypress) now fails on one TodoMVC behaviour: editing a todo to an empty string and committing with Enter. The error is `NotFoundError: Failed to execute 'removeChild' on 'Node': The node to be removed is no longer a child of this node. Perhaps it was moved in a 'blur' event handler?`
+The external browser acceptance suite (real browser, Cypress) fails on one TodoMVC behaviour: editing a todo to an empty string and committing with Enter. The error is `NotFoundError: Failed to execute 'removeChild' on 'Node': The node to be removed is no longer a child of this node. Perhaps it was moved in a 'blur' event handler?`
 
-The previous `dom-identity` defect (render rebuilt every `<li>`, fixed in commit 1f6f0ad) is closed. This is a different, browser-only defect. Root cause: the edit-commit path is reached from two handlers. The `keydown` Enter handler calls `commitEdit`, which splices the todo and calls `render`; `render` removes the item's `<li>`. A real browser fires `blur`/`focusout` on the removed edit input during that `removeChild`, before the node detaches, so `isConnected` is still true and the `editing` class is still present. The `focusout` guard does not catch this, so it calls `commitEdit` a second time and `render` calls `removeChild` again on the already-detached node.
+Root cause, traced from the failure stack (`app.js:107` render removeChild, reached from `commitEdit` from the `keydown` Enter handler at `app.js:197`): a real browser fires `focusout`/`blur` on the removed edit input **during** the list-element `removeChild`, while the `<li>` is still connected and still carries the `editing` class. The `focusout` handler guards re-entry with `!li.isConnected || !li.classList.contains('editing')`, but at that instant `isConnected` is true and `editing` is still present, so it calls `commitEdit` a second time. `render` runs again, a nested `removeChild` detaches the node, and the outer `removeChild` then throws `NotFoundError`.
 
-happy-dom is lenient and does not throw on `removeChild` of a non-child, so the in-harness suite cannot reproduce the crash. The fix is product intent, not a hint: the reconcile (or the edit-commit) must not remove, or attempt to remove, a node that is no longer a child of the list. `features/edit-empty-commit.feature` pins this as a `@conformance` source check, because the in-harness DOM cannot reproduce the crash. QM authors the checker that reddens on the current code; Crew fixes the product from that spec.
+The empty-edit branch of `commitEdit` removes the todo but never clears the `editing` class (normal edits rely on `render`'s `updateItem` to clear it, but the removed item never reaches `updateItem`). The fix is product intent, not a hint: the empty-edit commit must end the editing state (remove the `editing` class) before the reconcile, so the focusout guard blocks re-entrancy. The earlier `todoList.contains(li)` guard on the render `removeChild` is necessary but NOT sufficient — at re-entrant-`focusout` time the node is still a child, so that guard alone does not stop the crash. This is why the prior `contain`-only pin stayed green while the browser still failed.
 
-This defect is browser-only and must not be forced into a failing in-harness product scenario. The `@conformance` source check is the sanctioned guard.
+happy-dom is lenient: it never throws on `removeChild` of a non-child and never fires a blur during `removeChild`, so the in-harness suite cannot reproduce the crash as a runtime assertion. `features/edit-empty-commit.feature` pins the behaviour as a `@conformance` source check, because the in-harness DOM cannot reproduce the crash. QM authors/extends the checker (`features/support/reconcile_safety.js`) so it reddens on the current code — it now requires BOTH (1) the reconcile removes only current children AND (2) the empty-edit commit ends the editing state before the reconcile — and greens on the corrected code. This is the sanctioned guard; the defect must not be forced into a failing in-harness product scenario.
 
 ## Standing state (this leg)
 
-The prior voyage struck `watchbill.json` as voyage-complete, leaving the `@conformance` pin inert. Re-established `watchbill.json` -> `edit-empty-commit-reconcile` targeting `features/edit-empty-commit.feature:An empty-edit commit does not remove a detached list element`. The source check (`features/support/reconcile_safety.js`) reddens on the unguarded `todoList.removeChild(li)` and greens on the fixed code; verified by a planted-red probe before re-watchbilling. QM re-runs the watch to confirm the acceptance build carries the guard.
+`watchbill.json` -> `watch1` targeting `features/edit-empty-commit.feature:An empty-edit commit ends editing before the list reconciles`. The source check reddens on the unguarded empty-edit commit and greens once Crew clears the `editing` class (or detaches the `<li>`) in the empty-edit branch of `commitEdit`. QM re-runs the watch to confirm the acceptance build carries the guard.
